<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Follow the Boys (film)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1944</span><span class="sg-chain-h">played by Charlie Spivak and his Orchestra</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Cowboy and the Senorita (film)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1944</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung by Dale Evans</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Bob Eberly and Kitty Kallen with Jimmy Dorsey and His Orchestra</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1944</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover; number one in the United States</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Say It with Music (A Touch of Latin) (Ray Conniff)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1960</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover; a worldwide hit</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Beatles, Decca audition and Abbey Road session</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1962</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover; the Abbey Road take is on Anthology 1</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Dalida</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1976</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover; number five in France</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Amoroso (João Gilberto)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1977</span><span class="sg-chain-h">bossa nova cover</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Romances (Luis Miguel)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1997</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Mona Lisa Smile (film, sung by Chris Isaak)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2003</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">English version (Sunny Skylar)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">English lyrics</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Quejas, o la Maja y el Ruiseñor, in Goyescas (Enrique Granados)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1911</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the piano piece that inspired it</span></li></ul></section>
